text:
claire li: quick report from trying the new edge-starter-mini (Next.js + LangChain + LlamaIndex) in the samplekit-lite monorepo: requests to /api/chat sometimes return 401s and the client keeps hammering retries until it OOMs.
robert m.: saw that too during demos. seems tied to token rotation — our fetch-retry wrapper rebuilds the Request but drops the Authorization header on subsequent attempts.
ashwin: dug in: @redwood/sdk-js and sdk-edge have slightly different retry codepaths. sdk-js preserved headers; sdk-edge creates new Request(origReq) but doesn't merge mutable auth context.
kai: filed infra ticket 3507 and added a tiny integration that simulates an expiring token: https://git.redwood/infra/issues/3507 — reproducer points to fetch-retry in @redwood/sdk-edge.
docs-bot: Issue 3507 opened by kai 1 labels: bug, reproducer, sdk-edge
claire li: mitigation for the sample: add an explicit header helper in the sample's client wrapper and document it. Most new devs copy the helper verbatim and get stuck.
robert m.: proposed helper snippet (works around SDK until patch lands):
```js
// samples/helpers/authFetch.js
export async function authFetch(input, init = {}, ctx) {
  const origHeaders = new Headers(init.headers || (input.headers || {}));
  if (ctx?.token) origHeaders.set('authorization', `Bearer ${ctx.token}`);
  const req = new Request(input, { ...init, headers: origHeaders });
  return fetch(req);
}
```
ashwin: for the retry path, suggest rebuilding with the same headers instead of relying on Request inheritance:
```js
const headers = new Headers(origReq.headers || {});
if (ctx.token) headers.set('authorization', `Bearer ${ctx.token}`);
const retryReq = new Request(origReq.url, { method: origReq.method, headers, body: await origReq.clone().arrayBuffer() });
```
kai: thanks. I'm adding a CI smoke test to samples/e2e that runs the starter under an auth-flaky proxy and asserts there are <=2 total attempts per request. That will catch regressions where retries lose auth.
claire li: also updating samplekit-lite README "Edge notes" section with explicit snippet and a brief explanation of why Edge runtime sometimes needs explicit header preservation.
robert m.: can we hotpatch the published starter template and push a 0.1.1 quick-fix? enterprise onboarding calls flagged this as "blocks setup" this week.
ashwin: I'll open PR 3508 to the starter repo with the helper + README change and add the smoke test to CI. tagging @claire for review.
kai: PR 3508: https://git.redwood/infra/pulls/3508 1 includes e2e test, README update, and temporary sample helper.
docs-bot: PR 3508 created 1 reviewers assigned: claire li, docs-team
claire li: will review tonight. follow-up item: add a one-line triage step to the onboarding checklist for SEs: "If Edge starter hits 401s, confirm authFetch helper present and SDK version >= fixed-release".
robert m.: great. once PR merges, we'll publish patched starter and add a short note in the release notes.
ashwin: added unit test in sdk-edge repo to assert headers persist across retry. hope that prevents a regression.
claire li: thanks team. small wins for DX 1 this kept tripping new users.
